                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2d8e5b05-0d93-44cb-aaee-f222ae5b426c",
                        "source_entry_id": "3ba7e8b5-681f-333d-8a8d-aa66431ecdb2",
                        "source_sense_id": "b93bbbe5-10ae-33ca-9862-6d7e22c1c605",
                        "source_sense_description": "Entzündungen hemmendes Hormon, das für viele Stoffwechselvorgänge zuständig ist",
                        "target_lang_word": "cortisol",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cortisol",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "88d10506-290b-3be0-9390-d072342cc2b3",
                                        "entry_id": "509501a3-2e37-37db-8d5c-8651e315718e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A glucocorticoid steroid hormone produced by the adrenal cortex that mediates various metabolic processes (such as gluconeogenesis), has anti-inflammatory and immunosuppressive properties, and whose levels in the blood may become elevated in response to physical or psychological stress. When used medicinally it is known as hydrocortisone."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3bf50762-dd99-45bd-a78c-e810946b7819",
                                                "sense_id": "88d10506-290b-3be0-9390-d072342cc2b3",
                                                "text": "There is experimental evidence showing that cortisol restrains the intensity and duration of the emergency reaction to stress, and catecholamines have been shown to enhance emotional memory in the amygdala (see subsection on \"Noradrenaline\"). Thus, individuals lacking cortisol would overstore traumatic memories ."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "87965792-8475-4a7e-a81e-216a3794dcf9",
                                                "sense_id": "88d10506-290b-3be0-9390-d072342cc2b3",
                                                "text": "“While chronic stress can lead to increased levels of cortisol in the body, those levels don’t usually rise high enough to create a moon face,” said dermatologist Dr. Rajani Katta, a clinical assistant professor at the Baylor College of Medicine in Houston."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5e2d1ba6-da32-4ba2-93b5-68eaed96a02a",
                        "source_entry_id": "3ba7e8b5-681f-333d-8a8d-aa66431ecdb2",
                        "source_sense_id": "b93bbbe5-10ae-33ca-9862-6d7e22c1c605",
                        "source_sense_description": "Entzündungen hemmendes Hormon, das für viele Stoffwechselvorgänge zuständig ist",
                        "target_lang_word": "cortisol",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cortisol",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3546b865-7599-39f5-b400-4ee5392740a9",
                                        "entry_id": "b9c377b5-acd4-3a8d-bec4-a6d996b1c5f9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Hormone du stress produite dans les glandes surrénales."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "74ef0dc5-621f-4748-93da-838c7cb79613",
                                                "sense_id": "3546b865-7599-39f5-b400-4ee5392740a9",
                                                "text": "Une insuffisance surrénalienne primaire partielle donne un tableau intermédiaire: l’élimination urinaire de cortisol est à la limite inférieure de l’intervalle normal ; de plus, le cortisol plasmatique répond à un test de stimulation court à l’ACTH."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "719cbc7b-0664-40d6-b13d-8615ee816ca6",
                                                "sense_id": "3546b865-7599-39f5-b400-4ee5392740a9",
                                                "text": "Le cortisol on l’appelle souvent l’hormone du stress, et c’est pas faux. Je suis sûr que les moines, par exemple, sécrètent très peu de cortisol."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "217cd435-b11f-454c-abb2-65f3e99ace97",
                                                "sense_id": "3546b865-7599-39f5-b400-4ee5392740a9",
                                                "text": "À la clé, une réduction de la fréquence cardiaque et de la tension artérielle, et une baisse significative de la production de cortisol et d’adrénaline, responsables du stress."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
